==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
{{etyl|la|en}} mode that affirms.

From {{m|la|modus ponendo ponens}} (roughly, “mode where affirming affirms”).

===Noun===
{{en-noun|head=[[modus]] [[ponens]]|-}}

# {{context|philosophy|logic|lang=en}} A [[valid]] form of [[argument]] in which the [[antecedent]] of a [[conditional]] [[proposition]] is [[affirm]]ed, thereby [[entail]]ing the affirmation of the [[consequent]]. Modus ponens has the form:
#: 1. If P, then Q.
#: 2. P.
#: 3. Therefore, Q.

